<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan explained out loud with a picture handout; he repeated the main points back. LDL 122 mg/dL at intake; at 37 a 10-year risk estimate is low and a statin is not indicated, so lifestyle and blood pressure control are the focus. HIV, hepatitis C and hepatitis B screening drawn today; consent read aloud. [S]<list><item>Tdap and the first hepatitis B vaccine dose today; second hepatitis B dose in one month.</item><item>Dental clinic for the decayed molar.</item><item>Results of the screening tests by phone, in a voice message he can replay.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hypertension, stage 2 (I10)</content>. Near goal on the higher dose; trace ankle edema from amlodipine, not bothering him. [S]<list><item>Continue amlodipine 10 mg and valsartan 160 mg.</item><item>Leg elevation after long runs.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>128/80 mmHg on treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Lipid screening and statin</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Total cholesterol 204, HDL 58, LDL 122, triglycerides 120 mg/dL at intake; statin not indicated at 37 with low 10-year risk</td></tr><tr><td>Prediabetes and type 2 diabetes screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Hemoglobin A1c 5.4% and fasting glucose 92 mg/dL at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Begins at 45</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Routine one-time screening for ages 15 to 65; consent read aloud</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>One-time screening for all adults</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Triple panel, recommended once for all adults</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 0, read aloud</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>In treatment for moderate alcohol use disorder; drinking reduced</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy drug use</td><td>Up to date</td><td>DAST-10 0 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco cessation</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Does not smoke</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tdap today; no record of an earlier booster</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dose 1 of 2 (HepB-CpG) today; dose 2 in one month</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>When this season&apos;s vaccine arrives in the fall</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Offered with the influenza vaccine in the fall</td></tr><tr><td>Dental care</td><td>Referred</td><td>Community dental clinic for a decayed lower molar</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Tdap vaccine; no record of an earlier tetanus booster; Hepatitis B vaccine (HepB-CpG), dose 1 of 2, recommended for all adults 19 to 59 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (2025); AHRQ Health Literacy Universal Precautions Toolkit, 3rd Edition (2024); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Three-month review in six weeks. Second hepatitis B dose in one month. Dental clinic as booked. Influenza and COVID-19 vaccines in the fall. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 1969-09-22: three-month review: blood pressure, liver tests and drinking on naltrexone. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

